Package: rze
Title: Calibrated Detection of Clade-Localized Diversification Shifts
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("First", "Last", email = "you@example.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Detects clade-localized shifts in net diversification on
    time-calibrated phylogenies of extant taxa, using a stepwise
    model-selection search over candidate clades with an AIC threshold
    calibrated against simulated constant-rate trees. Reports net
    diversification per detected regime, handles incomplete sampling
    through a sampling fraction, and provides bold, poster-ready base R
    visualizations of the result. The calibration step addresses a known
    weakness of uncalibrated stepwise methods, whose default AIC
    thresholds do not control the false-positive rate.
Depends: R (>= 4.0)
